    "primaryWitnesses": [
      {
        "ref": "2KI 19:2",
        "textualBasisJa": "He sent Eliakim, who was over the household, Shebna the scribe, and the elders of the priests, covered with sackcloth, to Isaiah the prophet the son of Amoz."
      },
      {
        "ref": "2KI 19:5",
        "textualBasisJa": "So the servants of King Hezekiah came to Isaiah."
      },
      {
        "ref": "2KI 19:6",
        "textualBasisJa": "Isaiah said to them, “Tell your master this: ‘The LORD says, “Don’t be afraid of the words that you have heard, with which the servants of the king of Assyria have blasphemed me."
      },
      {
        "ref": "2KI 19:20",
        "textualBasisJa": "Then Isaiah the son of Amoz sent to Hezekiah, saying, “The LORD, the God of Israel, says ‘You have prayed to me against Sennacherib king of Assyria, and I have heard you."
      },
      {
        "ref": "2KI 20:1",
        "textualBasisJa": "In those days Hezekiah was sick and dying. Isaiah the prophet the son of Amoz came to him, and said to him, “The LORD says, ‘Set your house in order; for you will die, and not live.’”"
      },
      {
        "ref": "2KI 20:4",
        "textualBasisJa": "Before Isaiah had gone out into the middle part of the city, the LORD’s word came to him, saying,"
      },
      {
        "ref": "2KI 20:7",
        "textualBasisJa": "Isaiah said, “Take a cake of figs.” They took and laid it on the boil, and he recovered."
      },
      {
        "ref": "2KI 20:8",
        "textualBasisJa": "Hezekiah said to Isaiah, “What will be the sign that the LORD will heal me, and that I will go up to the LORD’s house the third day?”"
      },
      {
        "ref": "2KI 20:9",
        "textualBasisJa": "Isaiah said, “This will be the sign to you from the LORD, that the LORD will do the thing that he has spoken: should the shadow go forward ten steps, or go back ten steps?”"
      },
      {
        "ref": "2KI 20:11",
        "textualBasisJa": "Isaiah the prophet cried to the LORD; and he brought the shadow ten steps backward, by which it had gone down on the sundial of Ahaz."
      },
      {
        "ref": "2KI 20:14",
        "textualBasisJa": "Then Isaiah the prophet came to King Hezekiah, and said to him, “What did these men say? From where did they come to you?” Hezekiah said, “They have come from a far country, even from Babylon.”"
      },
      {
        "ref": "2KI 20:16",
        "textualBasisJa": "Isaiah said to Hezekiah, “Hear the LORD’s word."
      },
      {
        "ref": "2KI 20:19",
        "textualBasisJa": "Then Hezekiah said to Isaiah, “The LORD’s word which you have spoken is good.” He said moreover, “Isn’t it so, if peace and truth will be in my days?”"
      }
    ],
